}
```

### Collecting InstancedMesh
InstancedMesh objects require special handling:
```javascript
if (object.isInstancedMesh) {
  // Each instance has its own transformation matrix
  const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
  for (let i = 0; i < object.count; i++) {
    object.getMatrixAt(i, matrix);
    // Process instance with its matrix
  }
}
```

## Transformation Application

### Local to World Conversion
```javascript
// Single vertex
const vertex = new THREE.Vector3(x, y, z);
mesh.localToWorld(vertex);  // Applies mesh's world transform

// Batch - apply matrix multiplication
const matrix = mesh.matrixWorld;
vertex.applyMatrix4(matrix);
```

### Computing World Transformations
```javascript
// Ensure all matrices are current
object.updateMatrixWorld(true);

// Get full world matrix
const worldMatrix = object.matrixWorld;
```

## Practical Workflow

1. **Traverse scene** to find all meshes
2. **Update world matrices** to ensure transforms are current
3. **For each mesh**:
   - Get geometry (may need to handle InstancedMesh specially)
   - Get world matrix
   - Transform all vertices to world space
   - Collect into OBJ output
4. **Apply coordinate system transformation** if needed

## Common Patterns with Complex Scenes

### Skipping Non-Renderable Objects
```javascript
if (!object.isMesh && !object.isInstancedMesh) {
  continue;  // Skip Groups, Lights, Cameras, etc.
}
```

### Handling Groups
Groups are organizational and don't have geometry themselves, but their transforms affect children.

### Matrix Updates
Always call `updateMatrixWorld()` before reading world matrices, especially when transforms are newly created.

## Example: Collect All Geometry

```javascript
const scene = createScene();
scene.updateMatrixWorld(true);

const geometries = [];

function traverse(obj) {
  if (obj.isMesh) {
    geometries.push({
      mesh: obj,
      worldMatrix: obj.matrixWorld.clone(),
      geometry: obj.geometry
    });
  }
  for (let child of obj.children) {
    traverse(child);
  }
}

traverse(scene);
```

## Resources
- Three.js Object3D: https://threejs.org/docs/#api/en/core/Object3D
- Three.js Matrix4: https://threejs.org/docs/#api/en/math/Matrix4
- Scene Graphs Explained: https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Scene_Graphs

