# Three.js InstancedMesh Handling and Conversion

## Overview
InstancedMesh is an optimization technique in Three.js for rendering many copies of the same geometry with different transformations. This skill covers understanding and extracting individual instance data for export.

## What is InstancedMesh?

### Purpose
InstancedMesh allows rendering thousands of identical geometries with different positions, rotations, and scales using a single draw call, dramatically improving performance.

### Structure
```javascript
const geometry = new THREE.CylinderGeometry(...);
const material = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial();
const instancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(geometry, material, count);

// Set individual instance transforms
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
matrix.setPosition(x, y, z);
instancedMesh.setMatrixAt(instanceIndex, matrix);
instancedMesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;
```

### Properties
- `geometry`: Shared geometry for all instances
- `material`: Shared material for all instances
- `count`: Number of instances
- `instanceMatrix`: Matrix4Array containing all instance transforms

## Extracting Instance Data

### Getting Individual Instance Matrix
```javascript
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(index, matrix);
```

### Iterating Over All Instances
```javascript
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
for (let i = 0; i < instancedMesh.count; i++) {
  instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(i, matrix);

  // Extract position
  const position = new THREE.Vector3();
  matrix.getTranslation(position);

  // Extract rotation
  const quaternion = new THREE.Quaternion();
  const scale = new THREE.Vector3();
  matrix.decompose(position, quaternion, scale);

  // Or use the matrix directly
  // ...process instance...
}
```

## Converting InstancedMesh to OBJ

### Approach 1: Expand Each Instance as Separate Geometry
When exporting each instance, duplicate the geometry and apply its transformation:

```javascript
let vertexOffset = 0;
let faceCount = 0;
let objContent = '';

const geometry = instancedMesh.geometry;
const positions = geometry.attributes.position.array;
const indices = geometry.index.array;
const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();

for (let instanceIndex = 0; instanceIndex < instancedMesh.count; instanceIndex++) {
  instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(instanceIndex, matrix);

  // Transform and write vertices
  for (let i = 0; i < positions.length; i += 3) {
    const vertex = new THREE.Vector3(
      positions[i],
      positions[i + 1],
      positions[i + 2]
    );
    vertex.applyMatrix4(matrix);
    objContent += `v ${vertex.x} ${vertex.y} ${vertex.z}\n`;
  }

  // Write faces (indices need offset)
  for (let i = 0; i < indices.length; i += 3) {
    const a = indices[i] + vertexOffset + 1;
    const b = indices[i + 1] + vertexOffset + 1;
    const c = indices[i + 2] + vertexOffset + 1;
    objContent += `f ${a} ${b} ${c}\n`;
  }

  vertexOffset += positions.length / 3;
}
```

### Approach 2: Combine All Instances Into Single Mesh
For memory efficiency, combine all instance geometry:

```javascript
function combineInstancedMesh(instancedMesh) {
  const combined = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
  const geometry = instancedMesh.geometry;

  const positions = [];
  const indices = [];

  const origPositions = geometry.attributes.position.array;
  const origIndices = geometry.index.array;
  const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();
  let vertexOffset = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < instancedMesh.count; i++) {
    instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(i, matrix);

    for (let j = 0; j < origPositions.length; j += 3) {
      const v = new THREE.Vector3(
        origPositions[j],
        origPositions[j + 1],
        origPositions[j + 2]
      );
      v.applyMatrix4(matrix);
      positions.push(v.x, v.y, v.z);
    }

    for (let j = 0; j < origIndices.length; j++) {
      indices.push(origIndices[j] + vertexOffset);
    }

    vertexOffset += origPositions.length / 3;
  }

  combined.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(positions), 3));
  combined.setIndex(new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Uint32Array(indices), 1));

  return combined;
}
```

## Important Considerations

### Matrix Order in OBJ
OBJ format stores vertices and faces separately. When exporting:
1. Transform vertices to world space using instance matrix
2. Apply global coordinate system transformation (e.g., Y-up to Z-up)
3. Index faces correctly (1-based, accounting for vertex offset)

### Performance
- Expanding instances increases file size significantly
- Combining instances requires more memory during export
- For many instances, use streaming or chunking

### Coordinate Space
Always apply coordinate system transformations AFTER applying instance matrices:

```javascript
// Example: Y-up to Z-up with -90° X rotation
const vertex = new THREE.Vector3(...);
vertex.applyMatrix4(instanceMatrix);  // 1. Apply instance transform

// 2. Apply coordinate system rotation
const temp = vertex.x;
vertex.x = vertex.x;      // Keep X
vertex.y = vertex.z;      // Y becomes old Z
vertex.z = -temp;         // Z becomes negative old Y (this is wrong, see below)

// Actually: (x, y, z) → (x, z, -y) for -90° X rotation
const rotated = new THREE.Vector3(vertex.x, vertex.z, -vertex.y);
```

## Example: Full InstancedMesh Export

```javascript
function exportInstancedMeshToOBJ(instancedMesh, coordinateTransform = true) {
  const geometry = instancedMesh.geometry;
  const positions = geometry.attributes.position.array;
  const indices = geometry.index?.array;

  let objContent = '';
  let vertexOffset = 0;
  const matrix = new THREE.Matrix4();

  for (let i = 0; i < instancedMesh.count; i++) {
    instancedMesh.getMatrixAt(i, matrix);

    for (let j = 0; j < positions.length; j += 3) {
      let x = positions[j];
      let y = positions[j + 1];
      let z = positions[j + 2];

      const v = new THREE.Vector3(x, y, z);
      v.applyMatrix4(matrix);

      if (coordinateTransform) {
        // Apply -90° X rotation (Y-up to Z-up)
        const temp = v.y;
        v.y = v.z;
        v.z = -temp;
      }

      objContent += `v ${v.x.toFixed(6)} ${v.y.toFixed(6)} ${v.z.toFixed(6)}\n`;
    }

    if (indices) {
      for (let j = 0; j < indices.length; j += 3) {
        const a = indices[j] + vertexOffset + 1;
        const b = indices[j + 1] + vertexOffset + 1;
        const c = indices[j + 2] + vertexOffset + 1;
        objContent += `f ${a} ${b} ${c}\n`;
      }
    }

    vertexOffset += positions.length / 3;
  }

  return objContent;
}
```

## Resources
- Three.js InstancedMesh: https://threejs.org/docs/#api/en/objects/InstancedMesh
- Three.js Matrix4: https://threejs.org/docs/#api/en/math/Matrix4
- Three.js Vector3: https://threejs.org/docs/#api/en/math/Vector3

